WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.123 --> 00:00:03.018
- This Monday I went to
my first ever Apple event.

00:00:03.018 --> 00:00:04.663
I've never been to an Apple event before,

00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:06.263
so I don't know what's gonna happen.

00:00:06.263 --> 00:00:09.083
I heard it gets pretty crazy
in there, pretty rowdy.

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:10.583
Here are some things I learned.

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:15.530
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:18.843
First of all, I looked a little different

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:20.403
from most people at the event.

00:00:20.403 --> 00:00:22.630
People have got on suit jackets.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.703
As you can see, I'm wearing a hat.

00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:27.543
They played some damn
good music at this thing.

00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:29.323
I feel like this is better
than the club right now.

00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:30.463
(dance music)

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.143
I'm the only person jamming to it though,

00:00:32.143 --> 00:00:34.807
so I'll take it.

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:38.687
This guy Kevin is pretty
bad at drawing a flower,

00:00:39.979 --> 00:00:41.906
but pretty good at developing software.

00:00:41.906 --> 00:00:44.124
Also, these people really
like their game of thrones.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.092
My man Kevin?

00:00:54.092 --> 00:00:55.712
His dog was ready to be picked up.

00:00:55.712 --> 00:00:58.292
- And I'm expecting to get a
call to see when he's ready.

00:00:58.292 --> 00:00:59.815
- [Voiceove] (mumbles)

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.892
- She's like, "Okay,
come pick the dog up."

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:02.692
(laughter)

00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:03.712
I'm still a little iffy

00:01:03.712 --> 00:01:06.012
when it comes to constant communication.

00:01:06.012 --> 00:01:08.412
- You can read full emails.

00:01:09.965 --> 00:01:10.992
- [Voiceover] You can mark them unread,

00:01:10.992 --> 00:01:13.310
or you can flag them,
or you can delete them.

00:01:15.679 --> 00:01:17.615
- Also, Kevin's daughter needs to be

00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:19.435
a little bit more responsible.

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:21.875
- Here's one coming in from Maddie.

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:23.915
Saying she's forgot her key

00:01:23.915 --> 00:01:25.115
and can't get in the house.

00:01:25.115 --> 00:01:27.434
- I mean, he's in the middle
of a presentation girl.

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:29.134
App developers are a bit more cooler

00:01:29.134 --> 00:01:30.254
than you would expect.

00:01:30.254 --> 00:01:32.294
They're always down on a fist bump,

00:01:32.294 --> 00:01:34.318
or compliment you on your hat.

00:01:34.318 --> 00:01:35.558
- I love your hat.

00:01:35.558 --> 00:01:36.498
It's so cool.

00:01:36.498 --> 00:01:37.738
- Thank you so much.

00:01:37.738 --> 00:01:40.713
However, you may have
some different opnions

00:01:40.713 --> 00:01:41.485
on some things.

00:01:44.976 --> 00:01:45.530
- Okay.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.330
- Ready?

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.530
One, two, three.

00:01:50.037 --> 00:01:53.613
And Photo Booth is still
the best part of a Mac Book.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.733
(loud beeps)

00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:57.593
(camera click)

00:01:57.593 --> 00:02:00.253
Also, there's now another
way for people to avoid

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.253
talking about their feelings.

00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:05.353
- And you can even send your heartbeat.

00:02:05.353 --> 00:02:07.453
This is an incredibly intimate way

00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:09.433
to tell someone you're thinking about 'em.

00:02:09.433 --> 00:02:11.713
- Now I don't have to
say I love you anymore.

00:02:11.713 --> 00:02:14.593
Also, Shazaam finally got
it's (bleep) together.

00:02:14.593 --> 00:02:16.393
- I see the song, the album art.

00:02:16.393 --> 00:02:17.493
I can see the lyrics.

00:02:17.493 --> 00:02:19.393
- Oh my God, it brings up the lyrics.

00:02:19.393 --> 00:02:21.273
It brings up the lyrics.

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:24.653
- Overall I learned that Apple
puts on a pretty good party,

00:02:24.653 --> 00:02:28.372
with surprises, thrills, and
a lot of badly drawn sketches.

00:02:28.372 --> 00:02:31.232
Oh and by the way, tech bloggers
can be kind of agressive.

00:02:31.232 --> 00:02:32.092
Okay?

00:02:32.092 --> 00:02:33.732
I almost took a laptop to the head.

00:02:33.732 --> 00:02:34.972
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:02:34.972 --> 00:02:35.932
Excuse me.

00:02:41.408 --> 00:02:46.035
(upbeat pop music)

